generators.bas:11:11: a string is not an int
      yield "x"
            ^
generators.bas:15:14: loops loops over itself: its for is inlined
      for x in loops(n)
               ^
generators.bas:19:39: a generator yields its values: it has no as type
  function both(n as int) as int yields int
                                        ^
generators.bas:23:5: yield outside a generator: write function g(..) yields T
      yield 1
      ^
generators.bas:28:5: a generator changes as it runs: keep it in a var
  let a = upto(3)
      ^
generators.bas:30:7: print takes numbers, strings and bools, not an upto
  print b
        ^
generators.bas:32:21: a kept generator owns its arguments: no mut
  var c = changes(mut m)
                      ^
generators.bas:33:9: a generator has next() alone
  print b.size()
          ^
generators.bas:34:5: a generator changes as it runs: keep it in a var
  let s = upto(4)
      ^
generators.bas:36:5: x is the loop's counter: it can't change
      x = 5
      ^
generators.bas:38:1: for over a generator takes one name, not mut
  for i, x in upto(2)
  ^
generators.bas:47:9: upto is no value: it is a generator
  let f = upto
          ^
generators.bas:51:14: next() takes no values
  print b.next(1) or else 0
               ^
generators.bas:52:1: upto is a generator: loop over it with for, or keep it in a var
  upto(3)
  ^
